course: dictionary
lesson: 14247
title: Negligence: when care is missing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Negligence is a noun. It means not taking proper care, so that something bad may happen. «The crash happened because of the driver's negligence.» The driver did not pay proper attention, and that carelessness led to harm.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The factory's negligence let poisonous gas escape into the river.» Nobody took proper care, so negligence must mean carelessness that leads to danger. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "The factory's carelessness let poisonous gas escape" still makes sense.
explain: In law, negligence has a stricter meaning. It means failing to take the care that the law expects, and this can mean paying for the harm you cause. Stories and news use the word to show that someone was careless and to blame.
fact: Negligence means not taking proper care, so that something bad may happen.
fact: «Negligence» can also be a law word: failing to take the care the law expects.
fact: Negligence is an uncountable noun, so we say "negligence", not "a negligence".
fact: Carelessness is a close synonym, but negligence often suggests that someone should have known better.
fact: Context clues such as «caused the crash» or «blamed for» show that negligence is a bad thing.
exercise: «The crash happened because of the driver's negligence.» What does negligence mean here? | *Not taking proper care, so something bad may happen | Winning a race fairly | Having lots of money for a car | Being very kind to other drivers
exercise: A lifeguard forgot to check the pool gate, and a child got in. Which word best describes the lifeguard's mistake? | Patience | Generosity | *Negligence | Bravery
exercise: «The company was blamed for negligence after the leak.» What does the reader learn from this? | *Someone was careless and is to blame | The leak was a secret plan | The company was given a prize | The company was careful and brave
test: «Her negligence left the back door unlocked all night.» What does this tell us about her? | *She was careless and did not take proper care | She was very careful with the house | She was on holiday far away | She was lost on the way home
test: In law, negligence means... | Taking a long time to finish a task | *Failing to take the care the law expects, which may mean paying for harm | Being kind to strangers in the street | Winning a fair case in court
exam: Which best explains negligence? | Shining brightly in the dark | Being careful with everything you own | Taking a holiday from school | *Not taking proper care, so something bad may happen
